issue.body:
Hi there! I'm wondering if I'm the only one who finds the behavior of this package a bit strange:

```go
package main

import (
  "context"
  "errors"
  "os"
  "strings"

  "github.com/urfave/cli/v3"
)

func main() {
  if err := (&cli.Command{
    Action: func(ctx context.Context, command *cli.Command) error {
      return nil
    },
    Flags: []cli.Flag{
      &cli.StringFlag{
        Name: "api-key",
        Validator: func(s string) error {
          if !strings.HasPrefix(s, "API-") {
            return errors.New("wrong API key format")
          }

          return nil
        },
      },
    },
  }).Run(context.Background(), os.Args); err != nil {
    println(err.Error())

    os.Exit(1)
  }
}
```

It seems that the default value validation is failing before the actual flag value is parsed. Since the default value will always be invalid, this validation function renders the app unusable, even when the correct flag value is provided:

```shell
❯ go run . -h

Incorrect Usage: wrong API key format

...

wrong API key format
exit status 1
```

```
❯ go run . --api-key API-123 -h

Incorrect Usage: wrong API key format

...

wrong API key format
exit status 1
```

Currently, the only option I have is to set a default value that appears to be "valid-like":

```diff
&cli.StringFlag{
	Name: "api-key",
+	Value: "API-<set-your-key>",
```

Could you please confirm if this is intentional or if it might be a bug?
